<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48245" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thūcȳdĭdes</span></b> ,
			is, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θουκυδίδης,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a celebrated Greek
				historian</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Or. 9, 30 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">65,
			219</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Brut. 83, 287 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. de Or.
				2, 13, 56</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 10, 1, 73</span></i>. —
			Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thūcȳdĭdīus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Thucydides</i>, <i>Thucydidian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genus (orationis),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Opt. Gen. 6, 16</span></i>
			. — <i>Subst. plur.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thūcȳdĭdĭi</span></b> ,
				ŏrum, m., <i>imitators of Thucydides</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Or. 9,
				30</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
